        "kind": "exit",
        "title": "Caught in the act",
        "description": "Master Sallow has been caught at the Heron with the King's grain, before witnesses who'll swear to it, and Kell has arrested him (or he's being held for her) for theft from the Crown, and for Prout's murder if the proof will stretch that far. The true book goes with him as evidence (Scrope gives it up once the Master is taken), unless it burned.",
        "closing": "Close on the arrest done by the book: Kell's proper words, Sallow's courtesy curdling into threats, the gang watching, Duchess growling at his ankles, the lavender. Land it on the player.",
        "result": "good",
        "exitKind": "progress",
        "next": "kings-morning",
